# The rigid groups of a topology and their kinds (D403,
# docs/constraints.md, Section 3), on topologies made in the test: the
# two rules on molecules of several kinds, with atomic numbers and names
# that tell nothing; what makes two molecules one kind; one case for each
# reason that leaves a molecule out; the facts of a kind; and the weights
# of the sites against the placement of Section 2, within a bound from
# the rounding of f64. The largest error is over a tenth of each bound,
# so the bounds are not loose: transposing two weights, inverting the
# ratio of the two lengths, or changing a sign fails the test.
#
# RUN: mdir-rigid-groups-test | FileCheck %s
#
# CHECK: kinds: 9 molecules in 5 kinds, none left out
# CHECK-NEXT: sameness: equal numbers, no tolerance
# CHECK-NEXT: left out: flexible frame, site not of constant weights
# CHECK-NEXT: facts: scattered, incomplete exclusions, outside exclusions counted
# CHECK-NEXT: bisector weights: 20000 frames of three lengths within the bound, largest error 0.{{[0-9]+}} of it
# CHECK-NEXT: bisector site: 20000 placements within the bound, largest error 0.{{[0-9]+}} of it
# CHECK-NEXT: linear site: 20000 placements within the bound, largest error 0.{{[0-9]+}} of it
